<title>USA: Semiconductor Packaging buys 2 chip plants.</title>
<headline>Semiconductor Packaging buys 2 chip plants.</headline>
<dateline>MAMARONECK, NY 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Semiconductor Packaging Materials Co said its American Silicon Products unit agreed to buy two silicon wafer polishing and reclaiming companies from Air Products and Chemicals Inc for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The two companies -- Garland, Texas-based Silicon Materials Service and Netherlands-based Silicon Materials Service BV -- had about $15.5 million in total revenue for the fiscal year ended Sept 30, 1996, Semiconducting Packaging said.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to close the acquisitions as soon as possible.</p>
</text>
